      "resolvable": false,
      "notes": [
        {
          "id": 2497350257,
          "type": null,
          "body": "> TypeError: unsupported operand type(s) for |: 'type' and 'NoneType'\n\nThis is a typing notation only supported on Python 3.10+. Python 3.9 is completely EOL in October 2025, is it easier to update it?",
